A||||2||JohnnyK||Belt way to hot. This normal?||||1||
Z||000000||JohnnyK||09-03-2000||06:47 PM||||After about 20-30 seconds of the engine running, my belt starts squeaking. I was checking to see it the alternator worked itself loose, but i could not touch the belt because it was burning hot. (Burnt my finger to touch it for a second). Is this normal? I posted a message about this before, but it seems to be worse than I remember it. What is causing the belt to get so hot, even before the engine?? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||09-03-2000||07:54 PM||||If the belt is sqealing and gets that hot in a few swconds, the belt is slipping.  If the belt is tight, one of the pullies must be frozen, and the belt is being pulled over a non moving pully.  Check to see if the alternator pully is moving or water pump pully or a/c compressor.  What else does the belt turn?||||reg||3
Z||000002||theogre||09-04-2000||03:18 PM||||Nope, Not Normal.<P>What Lar said..... getting that hot you likely have a pulley problem not a tension problem.||||reg||1
